1
00:00:00,100 --> 00:00:01,720
They prepaid this hotel room.

2
00:00:01,720 --> 00:00:02,556
The front desk said:

3
00:00:02,556 --> 00:00:03,580
"We're sold out."

4
00:00:03,580 --> 00:00:04,358
That same night,

5
00:00:04,358 --> 00:00:05,438
their new room cost

6
00:00:05,438 --> 00:00:07,221
$1,400.

7
00:00:07,221 --> 00:00:09,102
Nassau, the Bahamas.

8
00:00:09,102 --> 00:00:10,959
Kristine and Jimmy Dworkin,

9
00:00:10,959 --> 00:00:12,103
from California.

10
00:00:12,103 --> 00:00:14,193
Night one of an 8-day trip:

11
00:00:14,193 --> 00:00:17,072
a Courtyard by Marriott. Prepaid.

12
00:00:17,072 --> 00:00:18,976
At check-in... no room.

13
00:00:18,976 --> 00:00:20,352
The hotel was overbooked.

14
00:00:20,352 --> 00:00:21,664
Kristine says the staff were

15
00:00:21,664 --> 00:00:22,998
"pretty rude about it."

16
00:00:22,998 --> 00:00:25,088
Hotels often overbook on purpose:

17
00:00:25,088 --> 00:00:26,574
some guests never show up.

18
00:00:26,574 --> 00:00:27,480
So around midnight,

19
00:00:27,480 --> 00:00:30,034
they walked the streets of Nassau.

20
00:00:30,034 --> 00:00:31,044
One room left:

21
00:00:31,044 --> 00:00:32,813
a suite at Margaritaville.

22
00:00:32,813 --> 00:00:34,334
$1,400.

23
00:00:34,334 --> 00:00:35,589
For 1 night.

24
00:00:35,589 --> 00:00:37,352
They started emailing for help.

25
00:00:37,352 --> 00:00:40,064
Kristine says Marriott did... nothing.

26
00:00:40,064 --> 00:00:42,277
So they contacted NBC Bay Area.

27
00:00:42,277 --> 00:00:43,566
A hospitality professor told

28
00:00:43,566 --> 00:00:45,435
NBC big hotels usually pay

29
00:00:45,435 --> 00:00:46,875
for your first night elsewhere.

30
00:00:46,875 --> 00:00:49,452
Marriott's website, NBC found,

31
00:00:49,452 --> 00:00:51,322
only promises a new room...

32
00:00:51,322 --> 00:00:52,748
to elite members.

33
00:00:52,748 --> 00:00:54,884
Then Marriott agreed to pay them back:

34
00:00:54,884 --> 00:00:56,057
the $1,400,

35
00:00:56,057 --> 00:00:57,837
plus the original room.

36
00:00:57,837 --> 00:01:00,043
In hotel slang, being sent to

37
00:01:00,043 --> 00:01:03,166
another hotel is called getting "walked."

38
00:01:03,166 --> 00:01:05,430
Usually, the hotel arranges the walk.

39
00:01:05,430 --> 00:01:07,299
This time, the family did it...

40
00:01:07,299 --> 00:01:09,570
on foot.
